{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel","id":897941,"title":"Idea: Giving Predator's Taint only to the Gangrel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T10:17:03-07:00","id":897941,"title":"Idea: Giving Predator's Taint only to the Gangrel","content":"I have a idea which I'll bounce this off to see what you think...<br /> <br /> What about only giving Predator's Taint to the Gangrel or one of their bloodlines while the other clans don't have it? Since I thought it would be more fitting for the Gangrel or one their bloodlines due to a clan based on savagery and especially animalism (well especially their WoD incarnations) hence they're more connected to the beast than other clans which therefore it might make more sense. Although I'm not a big fan of Predator's Taint but I think there could be use of it if it's reduced to a single clan or bloodline that only has it to make them distinctive to the others.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts or ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-24-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:43:44-07:00","id":897975,"title":"","content":"There's no predator's taint in 2nd edition.<br /> Are you talking about 1st edition and using it as the clan weakness for Gangrel instead of the mental deficient mechanics?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:47:31-07:00","id":897982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=897975#post897975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no predator's taint in 2nd edition.<br /> Are you talking about 1st edition and using it as the clan weakness for Gangrel instead of the mental deficient mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I lived under a rock since I wasn't aware that Predator's Taint was removed entirely. I guess it's better off that way.<br /> <br /> It might be also best to toss Predator's Taint into one of the endless sea of Gangrel bloodlines and be done with it as if nothing in value was lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:49:30-07:00","id":897987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=897975#post897975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no predator's taint in 2nd edition.<br /> Are you talking about 1st edition and using it as the clan weakness for Gangrel instead of the mental deficient mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly they were suggesting Predator's Taint for a weakness.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel clan bane is pretty good, I don't know why you'd call it mentally deficient.<br /> <br /> But bringing back Predator's Taint brings back the problems with it in the first place. It might be appropriate for a bloodline of particularly territorial vampires, but it would probably work best as the drawback of a certain Merit or a curse bestowed by blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:51:54-07:00","id":897990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=897987#post897987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be appropriate for a bloodline of particularly territorial vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I'm thinking of since they could be NPC obstacles that the PCs have to face.<br /> <br /> Since I'm also glad it was removed in 2nd edition because Vampires are not dogs that bark over the fence when you pass by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-24-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:49:27-07:00","id":898038,"title":"","content":"&gt;<br /> <br /> Because in 1st edition, the mechanics of a Gangrel character's clan weakness was to make them deficient in most mental activities that entailed rolling dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:22:14-07:00","id":898076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=897987#post897987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clearly they were suggesting Predator's Taint for a weakness.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel clan bane is pretty good, I don't know why you'd call it mentally deficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental deficiency was their 1e Clan weakness. They didn't get 10-again on mental skill rolls and 1s subtracted from successes on said rolls. It sucked because it severely punished concepts that went against the dumb brute stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:29:01-07:00","id":898085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=897982#post897982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I lived under a rock since I wasn't aware that Predator's Taint was removed entirely. I guess it's better off that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they removed it entirely. It's kind of the inspiration behind the Predatory Aura and Lashing Out. Basically, in 2e vampires always recognize each other as such unless there is some power at work hiding their predatory aura. They don't automatically react violently to sensing another vampire's aura, however. But they can voluntarily flare their auras as sort of a challenge, which is a little bit like Predator's Taint, except it's strictly voluntary and the results only put the loser kind of on-edge instead of forcing them frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:14:31-07:00","id":898203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=898085#post898085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say they removed it entirely. It's kind of the inspiration behind the Predatory Aura and Lashing Out. Basically, in 2e vampires always recognize each other as such unless there is some power at work hiding their predatory aura. They don't automatically react violently to sensing another vampire's aura, however. But they can voluntarily flare their auras as sort of a challenge, which is a little bit like Predator's Taint, except it's strictly voluntary and the results only put the loser kind of on-edge instead of forcing them frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'll ask you this, now is it possible to either remove Predator's Aura/Lashing Out entirely or just once again throwing it into a particular bloodline while there's another Bloodline with a much worse curse or a &quot;amplified Predator's Aura&quot; that actually is Predator's Taint?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:21:33-07:00","id":898210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=898203#post898203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'll ask you this, now is it possible to either remove Predator's Aura/Lashing Out entirely or just once again throwing it into a particular bloodline while there's another Bloodline with a much worse curse or a &amp;quot;amplified Predator's Aura&amp;quot; that actually is Predator's Taint?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:12:21-07:00","id":898276,"title":"","content":"Removing Predatory Aura completely as a standard option is probably going to have a lot of unforeseen consequences in the 2e rules. Lashing Out is a risky, but universal way to counter act Discipline spammers.<br /> <br /> Having a Bloodline curse that makes Lashing Out more risky/etc. is very easily doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:23:55-07:00","id":898497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=898276#post898276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing Predatory Aura completely as a standard option is probably going to have a lot of unforeseen consequences in the 2e rules. Lashing Out is a risky, but universal way to counter act Discipline spammers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it's really useful for all manner of other things, from non-violent conflict resolution to asserting dominance and regaining Willpower.<br /> <br /> Lashing Out and the Predatory Aura was one of the best things to happen to Vampire, and none of the other games have really done the 'aura' that well in comparison, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> H<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">aving a Bloodline curse that makes Lashing Out more risky/etc. is very easily doable.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">One of our bonus Bloodlines makes ample use of Lashing Out.</a></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:56:43-07:00","id":901431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=898497#post898497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus it's really useful for all manner of other things, from non-violent conflict resolution to asserting dominance and regaining Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can Lashing Out be used to regain Willpower? Playing a Kerberos character I often find myself having less WP than the rest of the party during fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:21:15-07:00","id":901447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/897941-idea-giving-predator-s-taint-only-to-the-gangrel?p=901431#post901431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can Lashing Out be used to regain Willpower? Playing a Kerberos character I often find myself having less WP than the rest of the party during fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a Mask or Dirge that plays off of Lashing Out. Competitor, Seducer or Monster, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-27-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}